Subject: [PATCH 09923/11362] Fabrication-gate determinations record which gate
 version made them

565 artifacts carry flagged_adversarial=true. None recorded which gate
version stamped it or when, so a determination made under rules that have
since changed was indistinguishable on disk from a current one.
conductor_gates.py blocks downstream work on that field, so the stamp is
load-bearing.

URGENT PART OF THIS COMMIT: 1adaaabe0a committed the stamp_provenance USE
in adversarial_verify.py without its IMPORT (a conductor `git add -A` swept
a partial working tree). `--backfill --apply` raises NameError at that
commit. This adds the import.

MEASURED, both directions, read-only over 6,924 artifacts (nothing under
results/ was written):
- 200 of the 565 would draw NO critical flag under the current gate; 365
  still would. The prior ~200 estimate is confirmed exactly.
- 1,126 UNSTAMPED artifacts now draw a critical flag. 995 of those carry
  NONTERMINAL_DECLARED_ARTIFACT, a check added 2026-08-09 that has never
  run against history. That direction is the larger one.
- Downstream blocking is currently zero: the live roadmaps hold one
  gated_on upstream and it carries no flag.

CORRECTION TO THE BRIEF: --backfill --apply cannot correct the 565.
backfill_stamps skips any artifact that already carries the flag, so it
can only ADD determinations, never revise one. A regression test pins it.

MECHANISM: every gate write of the determination now records
flagged_adversarial_provenance {gate_version, gate_version_algo,
stamped_at, stamper}. gate_version is a SEMANTIC fingerprint -- source
parsed, docstrings stripped, AST re-unparsed, sha256 -- so a comment-only
edit does not move it and a logic edit does. Staleness is O(1) per
artifact, no gate run. conductor_gates names the staleness and still
blocks; it never silently re-verifies and never lifts a quarantine.

NOT DONE, deliberately, referred to the operator: the 565 existing
determinations are neither re-stamped nor cleared. Correcting them writes
results/, which is evidence. Proposal with blast radius and exact commands
in docs/research-notes/stale-fabrication-stamps-2026-08-25.md.

Spec: REQ-VERIFY-6601 + 6 SCENARIOs in openspec/capabilities/verification.
